println(b_asideend)
println(b_content)
println("<h1>Language tour</h1>")
println("<p class='section-sub'>Triad has two profiles. Triad-Core is the subset the machine code seed runs today; Triad-Full is the complete standard. Every example below says which profile it belongs to, so you always know what can be executed now.</p>")
println("<h2>1. Blocks, values and functions</h2>")
println("<p>Triad-Core has block syntax, functions in two forms, lexical scope, closures and recursion. The value of a block is the value of its last expression, and conditions are <code>Bool</code>: there is no truthiness and no implicit conversion. The arithmetic is on 64 bit integers with wrapped arithmetic, and the remainder keeps the sign of the dividend.</p>")
println("<div class='code-card'>")
println("function area(base, height)")
println("    base * height")
println("end")
println("")
println("square(x) = x * x")
println("fib(n) = n &lt; 2 ? n : fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)")
println("")
println("let n = 10")
println("    println(fib(n))")
println("end")
println("</div>")
println("<h3>Core values</h3>")
println("<p>The Core types are <code>Int</code>, <code>Bool</code>, <code>String</code>, <code>Symbol</code>, <code>List</code>, <code>Function</code> and <code>Nothing</code>. There is no float literal: a float of the full language is represented with Core values by the self-hosted implementation. Lists are mutable and their indexes start at 1, symbols are written <code>:name</code>, and the conversions <code>Int</code>, <code>string</code> and <code>Symbol</code> are part of the language.</p>")
println("<h2>2. Declared types and multiple dispatch</h2>")
println("<p>Triad-Full adds declared types and multiple dispatch: a generic function is a set of methods, and the most specific applicable method wins. Operators extend like ordinary functions, and functions are first class values.</p>")
println("<div class='code-card'>")
println("area(n::Number) = :number")
println("area(n::Int)    = :int")
println("area(p::Point)  = :point")
println("")
println("function +(a::Point, b::Point)")
println("    Point(a.x + b.x, a.y + b.y)")
println("end")
println("</div>")
println("<h2>3. Logic inside the language</h2>")
println("<p><strong>Triad-Full.</strong> Facts, rules, unification with occurs-check, backtracking and <code>solve</code> are language features, not a library. A goal on a knowledge base predicate is already a query, and the engine is iterative, so a runaway resolution ends with a budget error instead of a stack overflow. They are not in Triad-Core: the seed has no Prolog, the logic engine arrives with the self-hosted implementation (S1).</p>")
println("<div class='code-card'>")
println("fact parent(:tom, :bob)")
println("rule ancestor(?a, ?d) :- parent(?a, ?d)")
println("rule ancestor(?a, ?d) :- parent(?a, ?x), ancestor(?x, ?d)")
println("")
println("sols = solve ancestor(:tom, ?d) limit 10 depth 50")
println("</div>")
println("<h2>4. Code as data</h2>")
println("<p><strong>Triad-Full.</strong> Quote returns code, a macro receives code and returns code. Expansion is pure and it is not hygienic, so <code>gensym</code> is used for temporary names. The tree of the program is uniform, which is what makes this possible. Quote and macros are not in Triad-Core: they arrive with the self-hosted implementation (S1).</p>")
println("<div class='code-card'>")
println("macro swap(a, b)")
println("    t = gensym(:tmp)")
println("    quote")
println("        $t = $a")
println("        $a = $b")
println("        $b = $t")
println("    end")
println("end")
println("</div>")
println("<h2>5. Errors, contracts, budgets, traces and effects</h2>")
println("<p>These are part of the language and not of a library. The list marks the Triad-Full features: Triad-Core has no error value, no macro and no quote, and an execution error simply ends the program with the exit code 1.</p>")
println("<ul class='feature-list'>")
println("<li><code>Err</code> is a value with a kind, a message and data; <code>try</code> makes the error the value of the expression (Full).</li>")
println("<li><code>requires</code> and <code>ensures</code> declare pre and post conditions, checked at runtime (Full).</li>")
println("<li><code>with budget(steps = 10_000)</code> bounds the body and yields <code>Err(:budget)</code> when it is exhausted (Full).</li>")
println("<li><code>with trace</code> returns the trace as a value, not as printed output (Full).</li>")
println("<li>Effects are declared in the signature: <code>!io</code>, <code>!state</code> (Full).</li>")
println("</ul>")
println("<p class='section-sub'>Source: SPEC.md §5-§12, SPEC-CORE.md §3-§7, README.md.</p>")
println(b_contentend)
println(b_layoutend)
println(b_mainend)
println(b_ftrdiv)
println(b_script)
println("<script>TriadSite.mount('Tour')</script>")
println(b_bodyend)
println(b_htmlend)

