println(b_content)
println("<h1>Bootstrap</h1>")
println("<p class='section-sub'>Triad must run without Julia, or any other language, at any stage: runtime, bootstrap or build. BOOTSTRAP.md states the requirement, the chain and the milestones that make it verifiable.</p>")
println("<h2>1. Why the obvious shortcuts are excluded</h2>")
println("<p>The requirement rules out three shortcuts. Rewriting the kernel in another language would add a dependency. Keeping a foreign runtime inside a packaged binary is still that runtime executing Triad. Committing a binary seed produced elsewhere hides the same dependency. The only coherent chain starts from an interpreter handwritten in machine code.</p>")
println("<h2>2. The chain from S0 to S4</h2>")
println("<div class='code-card'>")
println("S0  seed: Triad-Core interpreter in machine code (handwritten, x86-64)")
println("     |  executes")
println("S1  complete implementation of Triad written in Triad-Core")
println("     |  includes")
println("S2  native compiler written in Triad")
println("     |  compiles")
println("S3  self-hosted native compiler, no seed and no other language")
println("     |  compiles")
println("S4  complete Triad: REPL, CLI, examples, conformance")
println("</div>")
println("<h3>What the seed must do</h3>")
println("<p>The seed interprets Triad-Core and not the whole language: it reads a file and parses the lexicon, evaluates with environments and closures, carries the dynamic values, offers the arithmetic primitives and the output to the standard streams, allocates with a bump arena and exposes the entry point <code>seed program.td</code>. Triad-Core is chosen because it is small enough to be written by hand and expressive enough to implement the whole language on top of it.</p>")
println("<h2>3. S0, the seed</h2>")
println("<p>The seed is a PE executable for Windows x86-64 of 25088 bytes, without a runtime and without libc: it imports only a few kernel32 functions and reads the program from the first argument. Its source is an annotated hexadecimal dump kept in the repository, so the executable is materialised with a system decoder and never compiled. The Linux port exists at its E0 stage, a minimal ELF that prints its banner and exits.</p>")
println("<div class='code-card'>")
println("certutil -decodehex seed/windows-x86_64/seed.hex seed/windows-x86_64/seed.exe")
println("seed/windows-x86_64/seed.exe conformance/core/cases/ricorsione/program.td")
println("</div>")
println("<h2>4. S1 and beyond</h2>")
println("<p>The self-hosted implementation lives in <code>selfhost/</code> and is in progress: it is the interpreter of Triad-Core written in Triad-Core, with a smoke test in CI but not yet a conformance run. The native compiler and the self-hosting fixed point have not started, and the parity with the Windows seed, the REPL and the Linux ELF port are the last milestones.</p>")
println("<h2>5. Fixed points and development tools</h2>")
println("<p>The seed never contains Julia and is not produced by Julia. S1 and S2 are Triad sources versioned as text. The repository does not require Julia, Rust or C to build or use Triad. The seed generator is a maintenance tool that produces the dump: it is not part of the chain, and the goldens are committed text files, so no test needs another language.</p>")
println("<p class='section-sub'>Source: BOOTSTRAP.md §1-§8, STATUS.md, seed/windows-x86_64/README.md.</p>")
println(b_contentend)
println(b_layoutend)
println(b_mainend)
println(b_ftrdiv)
println(b_script)
println("<script>TriadSite.mount('Bootstrap')</script>")
println(b_bodyend)
println(b_htmlend)

